       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum for adults of 3,200 mg/day, and the usual outpatient limit is 2,400 mg/day. At that dose the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum for supervised inpatient use)\n- **1600 mg/day** in total, divided into smaller doses\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
